{"results":[{"url":"https://senatordb.com/vote/111-1-376","final_url":"https://senatordb.com/vote/111-1-376","title":"Senate Vote #376 (111th Congress): On the Motion (Crapo Motion t… — H.R. 3590","description":"U.S. Senate roll call vote #376, 111th Congress, Dec 15, 2009: On the Motion (Crapo Motion to Commit H.R. 3… on H.R. 3590. Result: Motion Rejected (45-54, 3/5 majority required), 45-54. See how every senator voted, with party breakdown.","language":"en","text":"Roll Call Vote #376 · 111th Congress · Session 1 · Dec 15, 2009, 6:28 PM (ET)\n\n# On the Motion (Crapo Motion to Commit H.R. 3590 to the Committee on Finance) (H.R. 3590)\n\nA bill to amend the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 to modify the first-time homebuyers credit in the case of members of the Armed Forces and certain other Federal employees, and for other purposes.\n\nMotion Rejected (45-54, 3/5 majority required)\n\n45 Yea\n54 Nay\n\n## How the Parties Voted\n\nDemocrat 58 senators\n\n5 Yea / 52 Nay\n\n1 not voting or present\n\nMajority position: Nay\n\nRepublican 40 senators\n\n40 Yea / 0 Nay\n\nMajority position: Yea\n\nIndependent 2 senators\n\n0 Yea / 2 Nay\n\nMajority position: Nay\n\n## Crossed Party Lines\n\n* Evan Bayh (Democrat–IN) voted Yea while most of their caucus voted Nay\n* Maria Cantwell (Democrat–WA) voted Yea while most of their caucus voted Nay\n* Amy Klobuchar (Democrat–MN) voted Yea while most of their caucus voted Nay\n* Blanche Lincoln (Democrat–AR) voted Yea while most of their caucus voted Nay\n* Ben Nelson (Democrat–NE) voted Yea while most of their caucus voted Nay\n\n## Full Roll Call: How Every Senator Voted\n\n### Yea 45\n\n* Lamar Alexander (TN)\n* John Barrasso (WY)\n* Evan Bayh (IN)\n* Bob Bennett (UT)\n* Kit Bond (MO)\n* Sam Brownback (KS)\n* James Bunning (KY)\n* Richard Burr (NC)\n* Maria Cantwell (WA)\n* Saxby Chambliss (GA)\n* Thomas Coburn (OK)\n* William Cochran (MS)\n* Susan Collins (ME)\n* Bob Corker (TN)\n* John Cornyn (TX)\n* Mike Crapo (ID)\n* James 